WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.772
[g@The Tang Monk trembled with fear.

2
00:00:05.773 --> 00:00:09.003
The animals showed their fangs.@g]

3
00:00:09.004 --> 00:00:11.634
"Master!" cried Wukong.

4
00:00:11.635 --> 00:00:14.151
The monkey was running fast.

5
00:00:14.152 --> 00:00:20.896
He swung his iron bar, and the animals ran back into the forest.

6
00:00:20.897 --> 00:00:25.926
Wukong smiled. "Sorry for making the horse run, Master.

7
00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:28.903
I thought it would be funny."

8
00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:31.392
[g@The Tang Monk frowned.

9
00:00:31.393 --> 00:00:33.264
"It wasn't funny at all!@g]

10
00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:35.994
Those beasts were going to attack me!"

11
00:00:35.995 --> 00:00:38.686
[g@"Nonsense," said Wukong.

12
00:00:38.687 --> 00:00:41.444
"You never have to fear any wild animals.@g]

13
00:00:41.445 --> 00:00:44.984
You have three powerful companions."

14
00:00:44.985 --> 00:00:50.042
Bajie and Wujing soon caught up to them.

15
00:00:50.043 --> 00:00:53.047
They all continued along the road.

16
00:00:53.048 --> 00:00:56.920
The Tang Monk pointed to a building up ahead.

17
00:00:56.921 --> 00:00:59.390
"That looks like a Daoist abbey."

18
00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:05.383
"I'm sure the abbey's priests will let us rest for a while," said Wujing.

19
00:01:05.384 --> 00:01:10.621
When they reached the abbey, Bajie knocked on the door.

20
00:01:10.622 --> 00:01:13.044
Two priests opened it.

21
00:01:13.045 --> 00:01:16.393
[g@"I'm here with the Tang Monk," said the pig.

22
00:01:16.394 --> 00:01:18.215
"May we come in?"@g]

23
00:01:18.216 --> 00:01:21.302
The priests looked at the Tang Monk.

24
00:01:21.303 --> 00:01:24.569
"Our master told us about you," said one of them.

25
00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.217
[g@"He said you would travel past our abbey someday.

26
00:01:27.218 --> 00:01:30.143
Please, come in."@g]

27
00:01:30.144 --> 00:01:32.904
[g@"Who is your master?" asked the Tang Monk.

28
00:01:32.905 --> 00:01:35.110
"How did he know about me?"@g]

29
00:01:35.111 --> 00:01:38.866
"Our master is the Great Immortal," said the first priest.

30
00:01:38.867 --> 00:01:43.069
"He is very wise and powerful."

31
00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:45.907
[g@Wukong laughed. "I've never heard of him.

32
00:01:45.908 --> 00:01:48.631
I doubt he's very powerful."@g]

33
00:01:48.632 --> 00:01:51.667
[g@The Tang Monk scowled.

34
00:01:51.668 --> 00:01:55.462
"Show some respect, Wukong," he whispered.@g]

35
00:01:55.463 --> 00:01:57.802
The priests looked annoyed.

36
00:01:57.803 --> 00:02:01.778
"Our master is visiting friends in Heaven right now.

37
00:02:01.779 --> 00:02:06.166
If he wasn't powerful, he wouldn't be able to do that."

38
00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:10.497
[g@Wukong shrugged. "I used to live in Heaven.

39
00:02:10.498 --> 00:02:14.932
The place isn't that great."@g]

40
00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:17.633
[g@"Wukong," said the Tang Monk.

41
00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:22.727
"Please go outside and tend the horse."@g]

42
00:02:22.728 --> 00:02:26.272
[g@Wukong went back outside.

43
00:02:26.273 --> 00:02:31.195
Wujing went out to get the bags.@g]

44
00:02:31.196 --> 00:02:34.131
"May I use the kitchen?" asked Bajie.

45
00:02:34.132 --> 00:02:37.829
"I want to cook some food for the Tang Monk."

46
00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.905
"It's through that door," said one priest.

47
00:02:40.906 --> 00:02:44.375
He pointed to a door in the back of the room.

48
00:02:44.376 --> 00:02:49.196
Bajie went into the kitchen while the Tang Monk talked to the priests.

49
00:02:49.197 --> 00:02:53.415
"There's a ginseng tree behind the abbey," said one priest.

50
00:02:53.416 --> 00:02:57.079
"Its fruit takes ten thousand years to become ripe.

51
00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:01.770
According to legend, one bite of the fruit will make you live forever.

52
00:03:01.771 --> 00:03:03.819
Would you like one?"

53
00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:07.673
"A fruit like that is a true treasure," said the Tang Monk.

54
00:03:07.674 --> 00:03:10.665
"Will your master be upset if I eat it?"

55
00:03:10.666 --> 00:03:14.953
"Our master said we could give you one," said the other priest.

56
00:03:14.954 --> 00:03:17.416
"We'll go and cut one down."

57
00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:21.579
The two priests went outside.

58
00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:28.097
[g@A moment later they came back in with a tray.

59
00:03:28.098 --> 00:03:30.421
The Tang Monk screamed.@g]

60
00:03:30.422 --> 00:03:34.388
On the tray lay a tiny sleeping baby.

61
00:03:34.389 --> 00:03:39.674
"I can't eat that," cried the monk. "It—it's a baby!"

62
00:03:39.675 --> 00:03:42.697
[g@"It's not a baby," said one priest.

63
00:03:42.698 --> 00:03:44.799
"It's a ginseng fruit.@g]

64
00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:50.008
It only looks like a baby to you because you're a mortal."

65
00:03:50.009 --> 00:03:53.213
"Please take it away!" cried the Tang Monk.

66
00:03:53.214 --> 00:03:58.157
The priests tried to convince him that the fruit wasn't a baby.

67
00:03:58.158 --> 00:04:03.713
But the monk just shook his head.

68
00:04:03.714 --> 00:04:08.781
The priests took the ginseng fruit out of the room and into a hallway.

69
00:04:08.782 --> 00:04:12.212
"We shouldn't waste this fruit," said one priest.

70
00:04:12.213 --> 00:04:14.237
"No," said the other.

71
00:04:14.238 --> 00:04:16.157
[g@"It is too delicious and valuable.

72
00:04:16.158 --> 00:04:18.239
Let's eat it ourselves."@g]

73
00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.470
[g@The two priests shared the ginseng fruit.

74
00:04:21.471 --> 00:04:24.455
Bajie was in the kitchen nearby.@g]

75
00:04:24.456 --> 00:04:26.945
[g@He had heard everything they'd said.

76
00:04:26.946 --> 00:04:29.888
His stomach growled.@g]

77
00:04:29.889 --> 00:04:33.638
[g@"That fruit sounds wonderful," said Bajie to himself.

78
00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:38.989
"I want some too!"@g]

